==English==

===Etymology===
From the present participle of {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|afier|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|affidare|lang=la}}. Related to {{term|affidavit|lang=en}}.

{{rfp|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|legal|lang=en}} The individual witness whose statement is contained in an affidavit or sworn deposition.
#: ''Further '''affiant''' sayeth naught.'' (A centuries-old statement that is still used on some legal documents as the final declaration prior to the affiant's signature.)

